[Music]  okay so this is my spoiler-free review  of shadow and bone i will also be having  a spoiler review breaking out every  episode coming out  in the next couple days but for this  obviously no spoilers and also no  spoilers from the books here i will not  be talking about the books i have not  read the books i don't plan on reading  the books please do not talk about the  books anywhere on this  comment section so going into this show  i am usually a big fantasy fan and i was  excited because  i heard good things about the books ben  barnes is in the show  and it's netflix so you think okay it's  gonna come through  so for me i think this is a very mixed  show meaning it's good it's got great  and it's got awful and i think that it  has a nice blend of it all  meaning you're gonna get it in different  doses so i think like  really what i would say about this show  is that if you are a  hardcore fantasy fan you're gonna enjoy  the show and i think it's  totally worth a watch if you're not a  hardcore fantasy fan  i do not think this is gonna be one that  appeals to just anybody i don't think  it's something that like anyone will  watch game of thrones or  something like a stranger things or the  witcher it's not like that  you have to be okay with eye roll  moments and what i mean by that is  it feels a lot of time like something  you'd watch on that show like once upon  a time where  it's like that hip fantasy where  someone's got a cool hat on or  you're just like oh my god like it's  really  corny in moments but some people like  that and i think  they will like this but it's not just  that though it's not a preference thing  it's also a thing where  there's so many writing issues  especially the first half of this show  it takes a while to get going and that's  expected with fantasy a lot of  characters and setting up this world  but the problem is is the main plot from  the start is really engaging  but you're gonna have a b plot that's  like in the start not that great it  takes a lot of screen time which  kind of makes you zone out and then they  add a c plot that's incredibly  boring and useless and that really  starts making you zone out so it's one  of those shows where  every fantasy show is trying to pull off  a game of thrones did having all these  different  areas to tackle and make them all  interesting which is really hard to do  and this has like three stories going on  and two of them at least the first half  just  really drag and it takes away from  momentum in the main story  that's what's the most frustrating thing  about this show however  it has some great episodes when the  stories collide and the plots collide  they're great  and then when it's separate not so great  but the acting  great ben barnes amazing as expected and  then  the lead actress who plays elena is  fantastic  every actor across the board is good  there's no one here that you're like oh  they're not good so that's a relief but  where the show suffers clearly is in its  writing also  it's gonna have some sloppy camera work  you'll see in certain episodes which  i'll pinpoint  in my spoiler review and questionable  directing but  overall it's a very decent show and  i really think unless you love fantasy  or read these books  i'd skip it and if you do love fantasy  and run the books you're going to enjoy  it i think you will get enough out of it  so  i don't think it's something to run and  go watch but if you're looking to kill  some time i think you'll get some reward  to it it's not completely  bad or useless i was able to finish it  so that's a plus already and i'm super  picky so  i do wonder how book fans will react  because i haven't read the books i don't  know if they're going to love this or be  disappointed but  it did feel like it was a little too  reliant on the book as well to make up  for  stuff in the show where maybe as a book  reader you can have patience because  you're like oh this is going to pay off  because i know what happens but  a lot of those things we don't get paid  off in season one so as someone watching  it i'm like  okay where is this going and it's it's  not fair to expect it as an excuse like  oh well don't worry later in the book  that character gets better or something  it's like well it still has to be good  now for the show  so when you're adapting books that's a  big challenge tv show writers have and i  feel like they failed a lot  in those areas in this show and another  thing i have to point  is there's a lot of bad action in this  meaning cgi is fine  the planning the action is okay but the  actual action itself  is really lame like you'll see moments  where they're using magic or you're  supposed to like blow wind  but it's like a little speck of dust or  when there's an explosion like a barrel  kind of breaks it's very  like laughable so that's frustrating too  because when you have action sequences  you want to go full in you don't want to  pull back and i feel like  it pulls back a lot but overall my  rating for the season of this show is  going to be a 7.4  let me know down below if you plan to  watch it and then let me know when you  do watch it what you thought of it you  can also go watch my spoiler review and  comment there we'll  break it down a little more and talk  about everything but yeah i really want  to hear what you guys  plan to do about the show if you're  going to give it the time of day or not  and if you enjoyed this review i'd love  it if you could subscribe i review a  bunch of shows movies i also do  celebrity interviews so you don't want  to miss that  please follow me at steve varley show on  twitter instagram for more of me  and i'll see you next time

